>> title: Skillet Cornbread
>> category: Cakes & Loaves
>> tags: cornmeal, southern, skillet, buttermilk, oven
>> counters: Meat and Three, Smokehouse, Diner
>> aka: cornbread, corn bread, buttermilk cornbread, Southern cornbread
>> servings: 8
>> time: 40 min
>> pairs-with: chili-con-carne, boston-baked-beans, hoppin-john
>> step.2: melt in a cast-iron skillet in the oven 10 min
>> step.6: pour into the hot skillet, bake 450°F (230°C) 22 min

Preheat the #oven{} to 450°F (230°C).

Melt @bacon fat for the skillet{2%Tbsp}(25 g) in a #10-in cast-iron skillet{} in the oven ~heat{10%min}, until it shimmers.

Whisk @stone-ground yellow cornmeal{2%cup}(280 g), @baking powder{2%tsp}(8 g), @baking soda{1%tsp}(5 g), @fine sea salt{1 1/4%tsp}(7 g).

Beat @buttermilk{2%cup}(480 mL), @eggs{2%large}(100 g), @melted bacon fat{3%Tbsp}(40 g).

Stir @&(~2)dry mixture{}, @&(~1)buttermilk mixture{} together just until no dry meal shows.

Pour @&(~1)batter{} into @&(2)hot skillet{} and bake at 450°F ~bake{22%min}, until the top browns.
